/// Options that control how CodeDeploy manages Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling
/// groups during a deployment.
pub struct EC2DeploymentOptions {
  /// The Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling processes to suspend during the deployment.
  /// CodeDeploy suspends these processes before it deploys to instances in an
  /// Auto Scaling group, and resumes them when the deployment succeeds,
  /// fails, or is stopped. Valid values are Terminate , AZRebalance ,
  /// InstanceRefresh , and ScheduledActions . This parameter applies only to
  /// in-place deployments on the EC2/On-premises compute platform. If the
  /// list is empty, or if the deployment does not target instances in an Auto
  /// Scaling group, no processes are suspended. The service role for the
  /// deployment group must have permission to call
  /// autoscaling:SuspendProcesses and autoscaling:ResumeProcesses on the
  /// target Auto Scaling groups. If the processes cannot be suspended, the
  /// deployment fails before any instance is updated. If you suspend
  /// ScheduledActions , scheduled actions with a start time during the
  /// deployment are skipped and do not run after the process resumes. If
  /// CodeDeploy cannot resume the processes, the deployment fails and the
  /// processes stay suspended until you resume them with the Auto Scaling
  /// ResumeProcesses action. While Terminate is suspended, Auto Scaling does
  /// not replace unhealthy instances. If you suspend Terminate , configure a
  /// trigger that notifies you when a deployment fails.
  pub auto_scaling_group_processes_to_suspend: List[AutoScalingGroupProcess]? = None
}

